ter-Process\",\n    \"combined Intra-Process\"\n]\n\nsub_df = plot_df[plot_cols].fillna(0)\n\n# 2. Plot stacked bar chart\nax = sub_df.plot(\n    kind=\"bar\",\n    stacked=True,\n    figsize=(9, 5),\n    color=[\"#1f77b4\", \"#d62728\", \"#ff7f0e\"],\n    edgecolor=\"white\"\n)\n\n# 3. Numbers inside bars\nfor c in ax.containers:\n    ax.bar_label(\n        c,\n        label_type=\"center\",\n        color=\"white\",\n        fontweight=\"bold\",\n        labels=[int(v) if v > 0 else \"\" for v in c.datavalues]\n    )\n\n# 4. Totals above bars\nfor i, total in enumerate(sub_df.sum(axis=1)):\n    ax.text(\n        i, total + 0.3, int(total),\n        ha=\"center\",\n        fontweight=\"bold\"\n    )\n\n# 5. Calculate totals\ntotal_attacks = int(sub_df.values.sum())\nsingle_attacks = int(sub_df[\"single\"].sum())\ncombined_attacks = total_attacks - single_attacks\n\n# 6. Formatting\nax.set_title(\n    f\"HAI 21.03 test attacks: {total_attacks} total \"\n    f\"({single_attacks} single, {combined_attacks} combined)\",\n    fontweight=\"bold\"\n)\n\nax.set_ylabel(\"Number of attacks\")\nax.set_xlabel(\"\")\nplt.xticks(rotation=0)\n\nax.legend(\n    [\"Single\", \"Inter-Process Combined\", \"Intra-Process Combined\"],\n    loc=\"upper left\"\n)\n\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-04T14:02:34.624528Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-04T14:02:34.624787Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-04T14:02:34.872197Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-04T14:02:34.624764Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-04T14:02:34.871407Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 900x500 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":82},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"Naming note: the paper's Tables 1–2 list `P2_AutoSD`, `P3_LH01`, `P3_LL01`, while the released CSV files use the names below.\n\n**replace with: ['P2_ASD', 'P3_LH', 'P3_LL']**\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 3. Splits strategy\n\nFollowing the paper (Section 3.2):\n\n| **Split** | **Files** | **Attacks** | **Use** |\n|---|---|---:|---|\n| Train | `train1–3` | 0 | Model training (normal operation only) |\n| Validation | `test1` (first 43,201 rows) | 5 | Threshold selection only |\n| Test | `test2–5` | 45 | Final model evaluation |\n\nThere is no cross-validation: the split is chronological and the model is trained on normal data only.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"print(\"test1 has exactly VAL_ROWS rows:\", len(lab[VAL_FILE]) == VAL_ROWS)\n\ndef split_row(name, files, role, rows_limit=None):\n    d = pd.concat([lab[f] for f in files], ignore_index=True)\n    if rows_limit:\n        d = d.iloc[:rows_limit]\n    e = get_attack_events(d)\n    return {\"split\": name, \"files\": \", \".join(f.replace(\".csv\", \"\") for f in files), \"rows\": len(d), \"hours\": round(len(d) / 3600, 1),\n            \"attack_rows\": int(e.notna().sum()), \"attack_events\": int(e.nunique()), \"role\": role}\n\nsplits = pd.DataFrame([\n    split_row(\"Train\", TRAIN_FILES, \"fit scaler and model (normal operation only)\"),\n    split_row(\"Validation\", [VAL_FILE], \"threshold selection only\", VAL_ROWS),\n    split_row(\"Test\", TEST_FILES, \"final evaluation (never used to tune anything)\")]).set_index(\"split\")\ndisplay(splits)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-04T14:02:34.873574Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-04T14:02:34.873921Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-04T14:02:34.928522Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-04T14:02:34.873894Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-04T14:02:34.927771Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"test1 has exactly VAL_ROWS rows: True\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"                                 files    rows  hours  attack_rows  \\\nsplit                                                                \nTrain           train1, train2, tr